// The kit ships as CommonJS. Under webpack or Babel its default import is the
// Chatbot component; under Vite or Node ESM it is the whole module.exports
// object, with Chatbot as a property. Keep the unwrap: importing `{ Chatbot }`
// by name fails under Node ESM, which can't see the kit's named exports.

// Keep the window on screen when the browser is resized. The visual
  // viewport's resize event also triggers the check: mobile viewports can
  // settle to their final size after the window's resize event fired
  // (emulated ones never fire a second one).

// A window remembered from a larger screen must not outgrow the
          // viewport, even when no resize event arrives. Percentages resolve
          // against the containing block: the viewport, unless an ancestor
          // sets transform, filter or similar. The minimums are capped too,
          // because a min size wins over a max size in CSS.
